# Everything listed here is excluded from the build context: the archive the
# CLI sends to the Docker daemon before any instruction runs.
#
# Two reasons this file exists, and the first one is security. A COPY that
# swept up .env would bake the database password into an image layer, readable
# by anyone who pulls it. Excluding it here means it cannot be copied even by
# accident. The second reason is speed: a smaller context transfers faster and
# is less likely to invalidate the build cache.

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Version control ─────────────────────────────────
# Carries the entire history, which the running application never needs.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# ── Virtual environment ─────────────────────────────
# Built inside the image from requirements.txt. A host venv is compiled for
# Windows and would be useless in a Linux container anyway.
venv/
.venv/

# ── Python artefacts ────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# ── Tooling caches ──────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ── Tests and local notes ───────────────────────────
# The runtime image ships the application, not the suite that verifies it.
tests/
PLAN.md
CLAUDE.md

# ── Editors and OS ──────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
